# Agent architecture

This file is the architecture contract for `$project_name`.
Update it before changing loop, context, tools, verifier, memory, skills, sandbox, or task-progress behavior.

## Project profile

- Domain: $domain
- Target platform: $platform
- LLM provider: $provider
- Deployment shape: $deployment
- Multi-tenant: $multi_tenant
- User-installable skills: $user_installable_skills
- Long-running session: $long_running

## Axis decisions

- Loop shape: $loop
  - Why: turn boundaries, replay, retry, and audit must stay explicit from day 1.
- Context shape: $context
  - Why: stable layers must remain byte-identical above the cache boundary.
- Tool dispatch: $tools
  - Why: dispatch is isolated behind permission gates and bounded tool results.
- Verifier strategy: $verifier
  - Why: completion needs external truth, budget pressure, and model self-stop signals.
- Memory architecture: $memory
  - Why: prompt-visible memory must be frozen at turn start.
- Skill system: $skills
  - Why: skills are content; executable code is supply chain.
- Sandbox: $sandbox
  - Why: shell-class tools need OS boundaries before model-level trust.
- Task progress surface: $task_progress
  - Why: current execution focus must survive long turns, resume, and compaction without becoming long-term memory.

## Tool catalog

| Tool name | What it does | Sandbox? | Approval gate? | Wraps result? |
|-----------|--------------|----------|----------------|---------------|
| shell.exec | run shell command | yes | default deny dangerous ops | no for own stdout |
| progress.update | update current execution todo state | n/a | no | n/a |

Add every new tool here before exposing it to the model.

## Verifier signal

- Hard signal: `$test_cmd_display`
- Soft signal: `AGENT_TOKEN_BUDGET`, default `200000`, with 90 percent threshold.
- Give-up signal: no tool use and assistant text present.

## Out of scope

- Unscanned user-installable skills.
- Multi-tenant data sharing or shared memory files.
- Unsandboxed shell execution in production.

## Deviations from 10 Iron Laws

No approved deviations. Add a dated entry here before shipping any deviation.

## Operational targets

- max_turns_per_session: 50
- max_tokens_per_session: 200000
- max_cost_per_session_usd: 5.00
- max_tool_calls_per_turn: 10
- max_subagent_depth: 2
- max_stale_progress_turns: 10
- p95 turn latency target: 3000 ms
- p95 tool latency target: 5000 ms

